      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It:\n1. Builds a `CommandLine` with a null deprecated handler\n2. Adds a non-deprecated option `\"cL\"` (no values set)\n3. Queries it using a deprecated `Option` with the same key and a default value `\"cL\"`\n4. Expects the default `\"cL\"` because the option has no argument values, and verifies no NPE despite null deprecated handler\n\nLet me write an improved, more readable version.Now I'll run the compile check.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test uses a descriptive method name, collapses intermediate variables into a fluent builder chain, and adds a clear comment explaining the scenario — that querying via a deprecated option with the same key returns the default value when no argument is set, and that a null deprecated handler does not cause a NPE."
